      "side": 1,
      "message": "[error] Line 33: 🔴 `nb_lost_samples` is derived from `pkt-\u003epts - expected_next_pts` without a lower bound. On reordering/duplicate/clock-jitter cases this becomes negative, then flows into FEC decode size and buffer sizing, which can trigger decode errors or invalid behavior. Clamp to a non-negative gap (`gap \u003d FFMAX\u003cint64_t\u003e(0, pkt-\u003epts - expected_next_pts)`), and only run the FEC recovery branch when `gap \u003e 0`.",
      "revId": "58af4ef51dd7f26ef9b1ba976871dc10ea008efe",
      "serverId": "1e26b4c1-6b8c-47ff-9df7-501b633d3b5a"
    },
